    "q-52716": {
      "dom_id": "step-q52716",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "What are the smallest and the largest possible **integer** lengths of the third side of a triangle if the measures of the other two sides are $5$ and $7,$ respectively?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote by $x$ the unknown length of the third side.\n\nAccording to the triangle inequality theorem, the length of any side must be\n\n- greater than the difference between the lengths of the other two sides, and\n\n- less than the sum of those lengths.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Difference} & <x<\\text{Sum} \\\\ 7-5 & <x<7+5 \\\\ 2 & <x<12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe above inequalities are strict. So, $x$ can't be equal to $2$ or $12.$ Therefore, the smallest possible **integer** value is $3$ while the largest is $11.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-52716-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "The smallest is $1$ and the largest is $11$",
              "html": "The smallest is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"30\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and the largest is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"31\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-52716-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "The smallest is $3$ and the largest is $13$",
