    "q-53103": {
      "dom_id": "step-q53103",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Abe knows that he lives $13\\,\\text{km}$ away from Becky's house and $7\\,\\text{km}$ away from Chris' house, but doesn't know the distance between their houses. Assuming that the three locations form a triangle, what is the range of all possible values for the distance between Becky's house and Chris's house?",
      "worked_solution": "First, we let: \n\n- $A$ be the position of Abe's house\n\n- $B$ be the position of Becky's house\n\n- $C$ be the position of Chris's house\n\nLet's draw $△ABC.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14167682/assets/6bd1335abf25d1d10da4e514c8c422aed987ad0bc6ce2afe3a7875ff7d5556c0.png)\n\nWe know that\n\n$$\nAB=13\\,\\text{km},\\,AC=7\\,\\text{km}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the triangle inequality theorem,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB-AC & <BC<AB+AC \\\\ 13-7 & <BC<13+7 \\\\ 6 & <BC<20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance between Becky's house and Chris's house, $BC,$ must be *between $6\\,\\text{km}$ and $20\\,\\text{km}.$*",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-53103-a",
